<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Autoquip year income up 38 pct, holds div.</title>
<headline>Autoquip year income up 38 pct, holds div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 35.5	  vs 25.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.5	   vs same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.89	  vs 2.82</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.29	  vs 4.02</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.16	  vs 0.92</p>
<p>    Turnover		  94.45	 vs 79.35</p>
<p>Full name: Autoquip Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Autoquip, which is a wholesaler and retailer of car parts, said its dividend is payable to holders of preference shares. The group said, as in the past, no dividend has been declared on ordinary shares though it would be considered once the preference shares have been redeemed.</p>
<p>The firm said slower economic growth, a spiralling crime wave and a more competitive market would make trading difficult in the coming year. But the group added it anticipated a real increase in earnings growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
